WHY THIS LICENSE AND NOT MIT

The source data derives from Glazy.org, whose content is licensed
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The Glazy.org AI Use & Data Access Policy (last updated
3 December 2025) states that any dataset or model released from Glazy content
must itself be released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and that commercial AI training
requires a separate license from info@glazy.org.

ShareAlike obligations propagate. A permissive license (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD)
CANNOT be applied to this derived work, because it would grant downstream users
rights — including commercial rights — that the upstream license does not
permit the author to grant.

The GlazyBench benchmark (arXiv:2605.06641) is distributed under MIT by its
authors (Ziyu Zhai, Siyou Li, Juexi Shao, Juntao Yu). That MIT grant covers the
authors' own contribution to the benchmark; it does not override the upstream
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 terms attaching to the Glazy.org content from which the
benchmark was derived.

If you need commercial rights to this work, contact info@glazy.org for the
upstream data and the author for the code.

